            <a href="system.html" class="active">System</a>
            <a href="order.html">Order</a>
            <a href="contact.html">Contact</a>
        </nav>
    </div>
</header>

<main>

<section class="page-heading">
    <span class="tag">HARDWARE + SOFTWARE + AI</span>
    <h1>SYSTEM <span class="glow">ARCHITECTURE</span></h1>
    <p>
        InfraNova is a proposed intelligent infrastructure monitoring
        system that combines image capture, AI-based analysis,
        communication, and a monitoring interface.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <div class="container">

        <h2 class="section-title">SYSTEM <span class="glow">BLOCK DIAGRAM</span></h2>

        <p class="section-subtitle">
            The following diagram shows the proposed flow of information.
        </p>

        <div class="grid">

            <div class="card">
                <div class="icon">📷</div>
                <h3>01. ESP32-CAM</h3>
                <p>
                    Captures images of roads and nearby infrastructure.
                    Camera placement and capture intervals depend
                    on the deployment requirements.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
                <div class="icon">🧠</div>
                <h3>02. AI Processing</h3>
                <p>
                    A trained computer-vision model analyses images
                    for supported categories such as potholes,
                    open manholes, or accidents.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
                <div class="icon">📡</div>
                <h3>03. Communication</h3>
                <p>
                    A suitable Wi-Fi or cellular connection
                    transmits detections and available image
                    information to a server or dashboard.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
                <div class="icon">🖥️</div>
                <h3>04. Dashboard</h3>
                <p>
                    Displays received reports, detection categories,
                    timestamps, and location information when
                    a location source is available.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>

        <div class="info-box">
            <h3>BLOCK DIAGRAM FLOW</h3>
            <p>
                Roadside Camera → Image Capture → AI Analysis →
                Communication Network → Monitoring Dashboard →
                Human Verification → Appropriate Response
            </p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-top:65px">
            HARDWARE <span class="glow">COMPONENTS</span>
        </h2>

        <p class="section-subtitle">
            The components below describe a possible prototype
            configuration. Final components depend on the selected
            monitoring features.
        </p>

        <div class="grid">

            <div class="card">
                <h3>ESP32-CAM</h3>
                <p>
                    Captures visual information from a selected
                    infrastructure location.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
                <h3>Power Supply</h3>
                <p>
                    Provides suitable power to the camera and
                    processing hardware. Solar power may be used
                    where appropriate.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
                <h3>Communication Module</h3>
                <p>
                    Wi-Fi or a suitable cellular module can
                    communicate data to a remote interface.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
                <h3>Optional Sensors</h3>
                <p>
                    Soil-moisture, vibration, or other suitable
                    sensors can support additional landslide
                    monitoring experiments.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>

        <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-top:65px">
            SOFTWARE <span class="glow">COMPONENTS</span>
        </h2>

        <div class="grid">

            <div class="card">
                <h3>Embedded Programming</h3>
                <p>
                    Arduino IDE and compatible firmware can
                    configure the ESP32-CAM and manage image capture.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
                <h3>Computer Vision</h3>
                <p>
                    A trained AI model processes images to recognise
                    the supported infrastructure categories.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
                <h3>Web Dashboard</h3>
                <p>
                    A web interface can present incoming detections
                    and help authorised users review incidents.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>

        <div class="info-box">
            <h3>IMPORTANT TECHNICAL NOTE</h3>
            <p>
                GitHub Pages hosts this informational website; it does
                not itself run continuous AI processing or receive
                ESP32-CAM alerts. Those functions require additional
                firmware, an AI-processing environment, a server,
                and a communication method. Landslide prediction
                also requires suitable validated sensors or models.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="buttons">
            <a href="solutions.html" class="btn btn-outline">← Previous Page</a>
            <a href="order.html" class="btn btn-primary">View Product →</a>
        </div>

    </div>
</section>

</main>

